  "articleBody": "So, you've decided to remove your old bathtub – great choice for modernizing your space! But once that tub is out, what happens next is absolutely critical: proper waterproofing. This isn’t just a nice-to-have; it's essential for preventing huge headaches down the road. When you take out a tub, you're exposing an area that was previously designed to contain water. If you're converting to a shower, this area becomes even more prone to splashes and moisture. Skipping out on proper waterproofing or doing it incorrectly can lead to leaks, mold growth, and expensive damage to your walls, subfloor, and even the rooms below. Think about it: water can find its way through the tiniest cracks, and in a wet environment like a bathroom, that's a recipe for disaster. This is why a qualified professional is so important. They understand the nuances of wall framing, tile backer, and, most importantly, effective waterproofing methods. They’ll make sure the entire wet area is sealed correctly, from the subfloor to the walls, protecting your home from moisture intrusion. Don't fall into the trap of underestimating hidden damage or failing to plan for plumbing or electrical changes before walls are opened. HH Remodeling LLC makes sure to handle these crucial details. Ensuring a professional handles this step means your new shower or bathroom space will be durable, safe, and beautiful for years to come. For expert waterproofing and tub removal services, contact HH Remodeling LLC.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}